# 20-FIN / finance and accounting

**Goes here.** How the money works over time. Cash flow and the cash conversion cycle,
working capital and inventory financing, P&L structure and chart of accounts,
bookkeeping and inventory accounting, COGS recognition, tax registration and
remittance, forecasting and budgeting, payment processing economics including payout
timing, reserves and chargebacks, funding options, runway and burn, financial
reporting for lenders or investors.

## Why this module exists

The OS ranks by profit, but a cash-constrained brand cannot act on a recommendation
that ties up money it does not have for 90 days. Cash is a precondition on plays.

## Not here

- Per-order contribution margin and the profit formulas the ranking uses -> 06-MEA
- Configuring tax settings inside the store -> 05-SET
- Negotiating landed cost down -> 18-COG
- Whether to make a hire and what it should cost -> 21-OPS
- Amazon fee structure -> 22-AMZ
- Growth diagnostics spanning economics, offer and operations -> 99-multi

**The MEA and FIN line is the one that matters.**

```
gross profit per purchase                    -> MEA
the landed cost formula                      -> MEA
what counts inside COGS                      -> FIN and MEA, tag both
when COGS is recognised, which method        -> FIN
cash conversion cycle                        -> FIN
chargeback reserves and payout timing        -> FIN
```

Which costs count as COGS IS the gross profit formula the ranking engine runs on, so
those sources carry `modules: [FIN, MEA]`. Tagged `[FIN]` alone, the measurement
agents never retrieve them.

## Header

```
---
url:                   # REQUIRED. Never blank.
rights: public_reference
why:
modules: [FIN]         # add MEA for anything touching COGS or margin
jurisdiction: []       # IN | US | UK | EU | global   REQUIRED here
topics: []
tier:                  # a practitioner is 3, never 1
scope_hint: mixed
---
```

`jurisdiction` is the safety mechanism for this folder. A card about GST filing
thresholds is useless to a US brand and dangerous if retrieved for one. Use `global`
only for universal mechanics like the cash conversion cycle.

## Topics

cash conversion cycle, working capital and inventory financing, chart of accounts and
P&L structure, inventory accounting and COGS recognition, bookkeeping and
reconciliation, payment processing economics, chargebacks and reserves, tax
registration and remittance, forecasting and budgeting, purchase order planning,
funding options and cost of capital, runway and burn, financial reporting.

## Look for

Formulas with every term defined. Timing above all: days between paying a supplier and
being paid by a processor. Real payout schedules and reserve percentages. Thresholds
that trigger a registration or filing, with the jurisdiction beside them.

## Skip

Aggressive tax structuring. Jurisdiction-free tax advice. Personal finance.

## Output rule

The system never presents tax or accounting output as settled fact. It carries an
explicit confirm-with-your-accountant label.

## Scope mix

Real baseline: a chart of accounts exists, COGS recorded per SKU, inventory reconciles
to stock on hand, processor payouts reconcile to orders. Collect these baseline topics
early, alongside MEA.

